217
00:16:19,116 --> 00:16:20,043
Let's land this.

218
00:16:20,383 --> 00:16:22,043
You should now be able to say:

219
00:16:22,383 --> 00:16:27,634
Git data is refs and objects and travels
with clone, fetch and push; GitHub objects

220
00:16:27,674 --> 00:16:31,904
live in a database and are reached
with the browser, gh or the API.

221
00:16:32,244 --> 00:16:35,221
A mirror carries refs and
objects, and nothing else.

222
00:16:35,561 --> 00:16:40,727
Files under .github/ and closing keywords
are Git data that GitHub interprets.

223
00:16:41,067 --> 00:16:45,763
Effective access is the highest of base
permission, team grants, direct grants and

224
00:16:45,803 --> 00:16:47,438
ownership; nothing subtracts.

225
00:16:47,778 --> 00:16:51,688
Visibility and settings are GitHub
objects and change no Git object.

